## F01: Public Donation Page

### Description
A public-facing page that displays the NGO's cause and allows users to donate a predefined or custom amount.

### User Stories

**US-01.1**: As a **donor**, I can view the cause title and description so that I understand what I am donating for.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Cause title is displayed prominently (H1)
  - Cause description is visible below the title
  - Cause image/banner is displayed (if available)
  - Target amount and raised amount are shown with a progress bar

**US-01.2**: As a **donor**, I can select a predefined donation amount (₹100, ₹500, ₹1000, ₹2000) so that I can quickly choose how much to donate.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Four predefined amount buttons are visible
  - Clicking a button selects it (visual highlight)
  - Only one amount can be selected at a time
  - Selected amount is passed to payment flow

**US-01.3**: As a **donor**, I can enter a custom donation amount so that I can donate any amount I prefer.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Custom amount input field is available
  - Entering a custom amount deselects predefined buttons
  - Minimum: ₹1, Maximum: ₹1,00,000
  - Invalid amounts show inline error
  - Only numeric input accepted

**US-01.4**: As a **donor**, I can enter my name, email, and phone so that the NGO has my contact information.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Name field: required, min 2 characters
  - Email field: required, valid email format
  - Phone field: optional, 10-digit Indian number format
  - Inline validation on blur
  - Form cannot submit with errors

**US-01.5**: As a **donor**, I can click "Donate Now" to proceed to payment so that I can complete my donation.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Button is disabled until amount + required fields are filled
  - Loading state shown while order is being created
  - Razorpay Checkout opens after order creation
  - Error message if order creation fails

