## F04: Admin Authentication

### Description
Login functionality for NGO admin team to access the donor dashboard.

### User Stories

**US-04.1**: As an **admin**, I can log in with email and password so that I can access the admin panel.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Login page at `/admin/login`
  - Email + password form
  - Supabase Auth handles authentication
  - On success: redirect to `/admin`
  - On failure: show "Invalid credentials" error
  - Session persists across page refreshes (JWT cookie)

**US-04.2**: As an **admin**, I can log out so that my session is terminated.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Logout button in admin sidebar/header
  - Clicking logout clears session
  - Redirect to `/admin/login`

**US-04.3**: As a **system**, unauthenticated users are blocked from admin pages so that donor data is protected.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - All `/admin/*` routes check for valid session
  - No session → redirect to `/admin/login`
  - Expired session → redirect to `/admin/login` with "Session expired" message

---

## F05: Admin Dashboard

### Description
Overview dashboard showing donation statistics.

### User Stories

**US-05.1**: As an **admin**, I can view total donations count so that I know how many people donated.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Stat card showing total number of completed donations
  - Updates in real-time (or on page load)

**US-05.2**: As an **admin**, I can view total amount raised so that I know the fundraising progress.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Stat card showing total ₹ amount of completed donations
  - Formatted as Indian currency (₹1,00,000)

**US-05.3**: As an **admin**, I can view recent donations so that I can see latest activity.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - List of last 10 donations on dashboard
  - Shows: donor name, amount, date, status
  - "View All" link to `/admin/donors`

---

## F06: Donor Log (Admin)

### Description
A detailed table of all donation records.

### User Stories

**US-06.1**: As an **admin**, I can view all donor details in a table so that I have a complete donor record.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Table columns: Donor Name, Email, Amount, Date, Payment ID, Status
  - Sorted by date (newest first)
  - Pagination (20 records per page)

**US-06.2**: As an **admin**, I can search donors by name or email so that I can find specific donations.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Search input at top of table
  - Searches by donor name or email
  - Results update as user types (debounced 300ms)

**US-06.3**: As an **admin**, I can filter donations by date range so that I can view donations for a specific period.
- **Acceptance Criteria**:
  - Date from and date to inputs
  - Apply filter button
  - Clear filter option
  - Results show only donations within range

